%% P1 p.15 - sharding by aircraft registration + replication: booked on the owner, copied to the backup
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant I1 as instance1 (backup of CS-TPC)
    participant I2 as instance2 (owner of CS-TPC)
    participant DB2 as flightops-db-2

    C->>I1: POST /api/scheduled-flights {aircraft CS-TPC}
    Note over I1: ranking by SHA-256(name + "|CS-TPC"):<br/>instance2 (owner), instance1 (backup)
    I1->>I2: POST /internal/flights (SERVICE JWT, not retried)
    I2->>DB2: lock aircraft CS-TPC (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE)
    I2->>DB2: overlapping flights of CS-TPC? none
    I2->>DB2: INSERT flight + outbox task "copy to instance1" (one transaction)
    DB2-->>I2: commit - lock released
    I2-->>I1: 201 flight
    I1-->>C: 201 flight, X-Stored-On: instance2, X-Replicas: instance2,instance1
    I2->>I1: after the commit: POST /internal/replicas (copy, revision 1)
    Note over I1,I2: a 2nd booking of CS-TPC at the same moment (via either instance) waits for the lock,<br/>then sees this flight: 409 "already scheduled"
    Note over I1: owner unreachable (connection refused / circuit open): the backup books it (AP)<br/>owner reached but no answer in time: 503 "booking state unknown"
